For reference, I have summarized the calculation methodology for each asset below:

Acacia Mining

Resources – 0.05 Mt: 47 kt of measured and indicated resources plus 6 kt of inferred resources, equivalent to 53 kt / 0.053 Mt of contained copper, rounded to 0.05 Mt.
Reserves – 0.19 Mt: 186 kt of contained copper reserves, equivalent to 0.186 Mt, rounded to 0.19 Mt.
Production – c.0.03 Mt: Estimated based on 157.1 kt of 2025 copper concentrate production and an indicative copper content of 18%–22%, implying c.28–35 kt of contained copper.
Capex – N/A: No publicly disclosed remaining capex figure identified.

El Abra

Resources – c.6.10 Mt: Codelco’s attributable contained copper resource figure was grossed up from its 49% ownership interest to a 100% asset basis.
Reserves – c.11.20 Mt: Calculated on the same basis by grossing up Codelco’s 49% attributable contained copper reserve figure.
Production – 0.09 Mt: Based on c.91 kt of 2025 copper production on a 100% asset basis.
Capex – c.US$7,500mm: Represents the preliminary investment estimate for the proposed sulphide expansion disclosed in the March 2026 EIA. As this was disclosed after 2025 and remains subject to permitting and final investment approval, I have flagged the timing and preliminary nature in the footnote. Defer to you on whether we would prefer to retain the figure or show N/A for consistency with the 2025A framing.

Anglo American Sur

Resources – 84.30 Mt: Sum of the contained copper resources associated with Los Bronces open pit, El Soldado, Los Bronces Underground and Los Bronces Sur. The total is based on the underlying unrounded source figures; approximately 65 Mt relates to the two longer-term underground resource areas.
Reserves – 7.74 Mt: Sum of Los Bronces flotation reserves, Los Bronces dump-leach reserves and El Soldado reserves.
Production – 0.21 Mt: 164.6 kt from Los Bronces plus 42.6 kt from El Soldado, totaling 207.2 kt / 0.207 Mt.
Capex – N/A: No specific future capex amount was publicly disclosed for AAS.

Quebrada Blanca

Resources – 29.81 Mt: Calculated by applying the disclosed copper grades to measured, indicated and inferred resource tonnage, resulting in c.3.52 Mt, c.13.61 Mt and c.12.69 Mt of contained copper, respectively.
Reserves – 7.05 Mt: Calculated as 1,330.6 Mt of reserve ore multiplied by a 0.53% copper grade.
Production – 0.19 Mt: Based on 190 kt of 2025 copper production.
Capex – US$495–605mm: Represents 2026E projected capital costs on a 100% basis, comprising US$455–555mm of sustaining capital, US$25–30mm of growth capital and US$15–20mm of capitalized stripping.

